Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Single source of truth: build the explorer from
 reg_advisor's YAMLs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

reg_advisor is now authoritative. The explorer no longer carries its own
catalogue; it reads programmes/*.yaml from the reg_advisor submodule through
reg_advisor's own loader, and the page mirrors reg_advisor's engine.

- vendor/reg_advisor: pinned submodule (see .gitmodules); run
  'git submodule update --init' to fetch it before building
- scripts/ra_engine.js: faithful JS port of regadvisor_engine (eval_term,
  check_prereqs, carry_ok, unmet_count, four-bucket verdict) — verified against
  the Python engine, 344/344 module-verdicts across both programmes
- scripts/build_explorer.py: loads each programme via reg_advisor, embeds the
  curriculum + concession rules unchanged, and computes parity cases with
  reg_advisor's engine that the page re-runs (footer 'Engine parity' chip)
- scripts/explorer_template.html: renders from the reg_advisor payload; marks
  entry drives pass/fail/carry/concession colour (no click-to-toggle); 40%
  carries and concessions handled exactly as reg_advisor does; print plan;
  reg_advisor palette

Concession numbers now come from reg_advisor rules.concession (55/1/45) — one
place, no second copy. The old ce_advisory/catalogue path is superseded.
